---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Shahzaib"
  description="Shahzaib is a Full-Stack AI Engineer based in Pakistan, taking products from zero to deployment across AI, backend, frontend, and infra."
>
  <div class="pt-8 sm:pt-12 fade-in">
    <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl mb-6 sm:mb-8 leading-tight" style="font-family: var(--font-serif)">
      About
    </h1>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 sm:gap-8 text-[#374151] leading-relaxed">
      <div class="fade-in fade-in-delay-1">
        <p>
          I'm Shahzaib, a Full-Stack AI Engineer based in Pakistan.
          I take products from zero to deployment, architecture, backend, frontend,
          AI systems, infra, and CI/CD. I've done this across hospitality, legal,
          governance, voice AI, and edtech.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Beyond writing code, I do product research, break down features into sprint
          plans, and lead dev teams to ship. I'm comfortable owning a product end-to-end
          or plugging into an existing team as a technical lead.
        </p>
        <!-- <p>
          Currently, I'm running{' '}
          <a
            href="https://baseera.io"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-[var(--color-ink)] underline underline-offset-2 hover:opacity-70 transition-opacity"
          >
            Baseera Labs
          </a>{' '}
          — an AI-first software company focused on product engineering and consulting.
          We build intelligent software that solves real problems.
        </p> -->
      </div>

      <div class="fade-in fade-in-delay-2">
        <h2 class="text-xl mb-3 font-medium">What I'm building</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          <strong class="font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]">Simplora.ai</strong>
          : AI meeting management. Pre-meeting briefs, real-time summaries, automatic
          action item extraction. Helping teams run meetings that actually lead somewhere.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-2">
          <strong class="font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]">DreamdeskAI</strong>
          : Enterprise AI for hospitality. Handles end-to-end guest conversation flows
          across every channel; email, WhatsApp, voice calls, SMS, and web chat.
          Integrates directly with PMS platforms to manage reservations and auto-generate
          staff tasks from guest requests.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="fade-in fade-in-delay-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl mb-3 font-medium">Background</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          I studied Computer Science at NUCES (FAST), graduating in 2024. During
          my studies I published first-author research on LLM-assisted property
          generation for Solidity smart contracts, exploring how AI can strengthen
          software verification.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="fade-in fade-in-delay-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl mb-3 font-medium">Stack & how I work</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          I work across the full stack and own deployment end-to-end:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-none flex flex-col gap-1 mb-3 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium">Backend</strong> — FastAPI, Node.js, gRPC, REST</li>
          <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium">Frontend</strong> — Next.js, React, TypeScript</li>
          <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium">AI / Agents</strong> — LangChain, LangGraph, Llama Index, RAG, Voice AI (VAPI, LiveKit), AWS Bedrock, MCP servers</li>
          <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium">Infra & DevOps</strong> — Docker, GCP, AWS EC2/S3, Nginx, GitHub Actions CI/CD, Digital Ocean</li>
          <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium">Databases</strong> — PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Redis, Supabase, Pinecone, pgvector</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          I also do product research, write technical specs, and translate them into
          sprint plans for dev teams. Outside of building, I follow AI/ML research
          and think a lot about what software engineering looks like when LLMs are
          first-class collaborators.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Contact -->
    <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-[var(--color-border)] pb-10 fade-in fade-in-delay-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl mb-3 font-medium">Get in touch</h2>
      <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] mb-6">
        Want to collaborate, discuss AI, or just say hi?
      </p>
      <div class="flex items-center flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          href="mailto:hello@shahzaib.ai"
          class="text-sm px-4 py-2 rounded-md border border-[var(--color-ink)] text-[var(--color-ink)] hover:bg-[var(--color-ink)] hover:text-[var(--color-cream)] transition-colors font-medium"
        >
          hello@shahzaib.ai
        </a>
        <a
          href=""
          onclick="Calendly.initPopupWidget({url:'https://calendly.com/shahzaib-khan0217/30min?hide_gdpr_banner=1'});return false;"
          class="text-sm px-4 py-2 rounded-md bg-[var(--color-ink)] text-[var(--color-cream)] hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity font-medium"
        >
          book a call
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
